{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QJYLz9PmodVbpHVhpYRaJS","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"d0f4b1bf5be04ad6f9c567635864b36de6ac36c3","date":"2026-10-07T13:20:03.000Z","author":"Veronica Mukuhi Muthee","subject":"(feat) O3-5823: Capture diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note (#3621)","message":"(feat) O3-5823: Capture diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note (#3621)","ticketKeys":["O3-5823"],"pullRequests":[3621],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"a0834be003ea69917f36dac8b4bccba52ba8a7a4","date":"2026-10-02T05:50:44.000Z","author":"chibongho","subject":"(fix) O3-6020: Make Visit Notes workspace accept an Encounter object for editing (#3719)","message":"(fix) O3-6020: Make Visit Notes workspace accept an Encounter object for editing (#3719)\n\n* (fix) O3-6020: Make Visit Notes workspace accept a Encounter object for editing\n\n* address feedback\n\n---------","ticketKeys":["O3-6020"],"pullRequests":[3719],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"108c48985b5e33905d025cb936a5657f45bb7a7a","date":"2026-09-24T20:50:01.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5998: Continue to the requested workspace after starting or selecting a visit (#3688)","message":"(fix) O3-5998: Continue to the requested workspace after starting or selecting a visit (#3688)\n\n* (fix) O3-5998: Continue to the requested workspace after starting or selecting a visit\n\nWhen a chart action needs a visit and the patient has none,\nuseStartVisitIfNeeded shows a visit prompt and waits for the user to start\nor pick a visit. Neither path continued to the workspace the user asked\nfor, so they had to click the action again.\n\nWith RDE off, the start visit dialog passes onVisitStarted into the\nstart-visit-workspace-form workspace, but the chart's wrapper for that\nworkspace never read it, so the promise never resolved. The wrapper now\naccepts onVisitStarted and calls it after it sets the visit context.\n\nWith RDE on, selecting a visit resolved the promise straight away. Setting\na new visit context makes the patient chart relaunch its workspace group\nonce the visit is refetched, and the relaunch closes every open window, so\nthe resumed workspace was closed before it rendered. The RDE-off path\nwould hit the same thing once the callback is wired up.\n\nThe patient chart store now records which visit the workspace group was\nlast launched with, and the chart sets it after each successful relaunch.\nuseStartVisitIfNeeded resolves true only once that matches the new visit\ncontext. Under RDE, closing the switcher after a selection no longer\nresolves false first.\n\n* Check that the visit note opens after starting a visit from the prompt\n\nThe visit context test already opens the visit note from the side rail\nwith no visit, starts a visit from the prompt, and waits for the Active\nVisit tag. It now also checks that the visit note form opens by itself\nand can still be written in once the chart has picked up the new visit,\nthen discards the note so the later delete visit steps start clean.\n\n* Resolve every pending visit prompt once the workspace group has the visit\n\nuseStartVisitIfNeeded kept a single pending resolver per hook instance, so\nif the same caller had two prompts comp","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-5998"],"pullRequests":[3688],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"4d9f19a2d629347559fe32b89899af6245c16e23","date":"2026-09-24T15:31:10.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5989: Keep a visit note saved when one of its images is rejected (#3670)","message":"(fix) O3-5989: Keep a visit note saved when one of its images is rejected (#3670)\n\nBy the time the images upload, the note and its diagnoses are already on\nthe server. A rejected image used to bubble into the catch handler, which\nshowed \"Error saving visit note\" and left the form open in create mode, so\nthe next Save and close posted a second note.\n\nUploads now run with Promise.allSettled. Every image the server accepts is\nsaved, the workspace closes as usual, and a warning snackbar names the\nimages that were rejected with the server's reason, pointing the user at\nthe note to add them again. A failure to save the note itself still shows\nthe error and keeps the form open.","ticketKeys":["O3-5989"],"pullRequests":[3670],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"52ad5642b88661b759f5e130f12e1d73a7fac66a","date":"2026-09-23T08:32:38.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)","message":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)\n\n* fix: O3-5990 Remove saved visit-note images safely\n\nConfirm removal of a saved image and void its observation through the obs endpoint. This preserves the encounter and diagnoses when the image is the only observation. Refresh attachment, note, and visit data after removal.\n\nExplain that removal takes effect immediately and discarding note edits will not restore the image. Cover cancel, success, and retry after failure. Verify that a blank note and its diagnosis survive removal of the sole image in the local browser and backend.\n\n* style: Put React first in image removal test imports\n\nMove the React import above the test utilities in the saved-image removal modal test.\n\n* fix: Save visit-note image removals with the form\n\nKeep image removals pending until Save and close, with Undo and Discard restoring the draft. Show a dimmed thumbnail and a separate Undo action for images marked for removal.\n\nRetry failed removals without repeating successful deletions, and avoid rewriting the note when only images change. Keep the visit-context header state stable during form updates.\n\n* fix: Refresh visit-note data once per save attempt\n\nRefresh after the removal batch and note save, including partial failures. Add coverage for saved diagnoses and successful and failed removal batches.\n\nSimplify the image markup, separate the error title from its explanation, and remove redundant footer styles.","ticketKeys":["O3-5990"],"pullRequests":[3684],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"96b812bb0206c034792895cacfad69dd3f37b44a","date":"2026-09-18T20:42:17.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5986: Show a visit note's saved images when editing it (#3668)","message":"(fix) O3-5986: Show a visit note's saved images when editing it (#3668)\n\nImages added to a visit note are uploaded with the note's encounter UUID, and the edit form loads and shows the attachments recorded on that encounter, read only. Only images added in the session live in form state, so a text-only edit uploads nothing. Attachment obs in the Visits page encounter expansion render as caption or file-name links that open a new read-only attachment-preview-modal, and the bytes URL helper moves to esm-patient-common-lib. Depends on openmrs/openmrs-esm-core#1887. Follow-ups: O3-5987, O3-5988, O3-5989, O3-5990.","ticketKeys":["O3-5986","O3-5987","O3-5988","O3-5989","O3-5990"],"pullRequests":[3668],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"385d75cc2bbcc2a6802ca4f96dde611072cd4dec","date":"2026-09-17T18:05:49.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls (#3663)","message":"(fix) Preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls (#3663)\n\n* fix: preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls\n\nTrack image additions and removals as form changes and read the current images for each upload callback so batches retain every file. Use labelled, contrasting remove buttons that do not submit the form. Cover create and edit workflows, batch uploads and removal.\n\n* fix: preserve image remove button contrast across interaction states\n\nSet explicit hover, focus and active colours so Carbon secondary button styles cannot hide the close icon. Remove the redundant button type, which Carbon already defaults to button.\n\n* fix: identify images in visit note removal labels\n\nUse the image description, filename or image number in each remove button's accessible name. Update the translation and tests to cover the fallbacks and select the intended image by name.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3663],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e8bf5eeaa08a65b4b8b1845e4ca1a224f3f90790","date":"2026-09-14T10:31:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)","message":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)\n\n* (fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form\n\nMake condition search results keyboard accessible with visible focus and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep the selected condition name in the input.\n\nUse Record condition for creation and Edit condition for editing. Update translations and cover keyboard navigation and workspace titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Remove unused conditions workspace title prop\n\nThe conditions form sets its edit title on Workspace2. Remove the unused launch prop and translation dependency, and update the action menu test to match.\n\n* Keep condition search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the search input when loading removes a focused result. Leave focus alone when the user has moved elsewhere, and test that keyboard input continues in the intended field.","ticketKeys":["O3-5969"],"pullRequests":[3646],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6961c3d13e74a69bc2ed96dc3fa5aa1cc4d86f25","date":"2026-09-11T21:11:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)","message":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)\n\n* (fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes\n\nMake diagnosis search results keyboard accessible and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep tablet row padding on the result button so its click target and focus outline fill the row.\n\nUse Add visit note and Edit visit note consistently in workspace titles and tablet headings. Update translations and cover the keyboard flow and titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Update visit context test for the add visit note title\n\nThe siderail opens the note workspace in creation mode. Expect Add visit note so the visit context test matches the renamed workspace title.\n\n* Keep diagnosis search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the corresponding diagnosis input when loading removes a focused result. Preserve focus when the user moves elsewhere, and cover continued typing in both diagnosis searches and the notes field.\n\n* Reduce spacing below open diagnosis results\n\nUse a smaller bottom margin while diagnosis results are visible. Keep the existing spacing when the list is closed. Verified desktop and tablet layouts and the visit-note E2E workflow.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3645],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"324603e9b2d62756416654585d2e6c1d1653fa14","date":"2026-09-01T20:29:42.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)","message":"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)\n\n* (fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label\n\nOn @carbon/react 1.x, the classic OverflowMenu pulls aria-label out of its props and applies it to the menu body (the ul with role menu), not to the trigger button. The trigger's accessible name comes from iconDescription, which defaults to 'Options'. Every overflow menu in this repo passed its label via aria-label, so screen readers announced a generic 'Options' for all of them.\n\nPass the label through iconDescription instead in the visit timeline, encounters table, orders and medications tables, and the allergies, conditions, procedures, programs, and vitals action menus. The conditions menu label was a hardcoded string, so it is now translated. Unit tests and e2e specs that located the triggers by the 'Options' name now use the real labels.\n\n* Keep aria-label on overflow menus so the popup stays named\n\nCarbon's classic OverflowMenu applies aria-label to the opened menu body (the ul with role menu), so dropping it left the popup without an accessible name. Keep aria-label alongside iconDescription so the trigger and the popup are both named. The encounters table test now asserts the popup's aria-label.\n\n* Disambiguate the delete confirmation locators in the e2e specs\n\nThe allergies, biometrics, and vitals trigger names now contain the word delete, so the modal confirmation locator getByRole('button', { name: /delete/i }) matched two elements and failed in strict mode. Target the modal's danger button instead, matching the existing conditions spec.\n\n* Cover the remaining overflow menu labels\n\nName the procedures, attachment preview, and clinical encounter list menus consistently. Remove the misplaced attachment menu item label and cover the accessible names in focused tests.\n\n* Update the procedures and attachments e2e locators for the new trigger names\n\nThe procedures and attachment preview triggers a","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3612],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"c6df9cf74c0b4e52986befd68a2fc9f19807bde6","date":"2026-08-18T14:03:07.000Z","author":"Ujjawal Prabhat","subject":"(fix) O3-5763: Let hosts handle encounter editing outside the chart (#3569)","message":"(fix) O3-5763: Let hosts handle encounter editing outside the chart (#3569)\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Let hosts handle encounter editing outside the chart\n\n* (chore) O3-5763: Cover both encounter edit paths in EncountersTable\n\n* (chore) O3-5763: Cover onEditEncounter pass-through and query by role\n\nAddresses review feedback on #3569:\n\n- Fold the edit-routing tests into the  block and\n  name each one for the path it covers (host callback vs the chart's own\n  workspaces).\n- Add cases for a form-backed visit note encounter and for the overflow\n  menu's edit item, not just the expanded row's button.\n- Assert VisitSummary threads onEditEncounter down to both the encounters\n  and completed forms tabs.\n- Query the overflow menu via  and the\n  expanded row's buttons at screen level, which drops the\n   disable from encounters-table.test.tsx.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","ticketKeys":["O3-5763"],"pullRequests":[3569],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"80db8ffc6ae52b7f708ed32aaa2f8a8b9abd4776","date":"2026-08-10T05:36:53.000Z","author":"Ujjawal Prabhat","subject":"(fix) O3-5763: Expose the visit notes form as a reusable workspace (#3509)","message":"(fix) O3-5763: Expose the visit notes form as a reusable workspace (#3509)\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Expose the visit notes form as a reusable workspace\n\n* (chore) Move visit note form implementation into visit-notes-form.component.tsx\n\nAddresses review feedback on #3509. The shared form implementation lived in\nexported-visit-notes-form.workspace.tsx, which made the in-chart workspace\ndepend on the out-of-chart one and obscured the architecture.\n\nMove it to visit-notes-form.component.tsx and make both workspaces thin\nadapters over it, matching form entry, add drug order and the order basket.\nThe component body is unchanged apart from its props signature.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","ticketKeys":["O3-5763"],"pullRequests":[3509],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"1a2af778aa7f86ea2c1fc944e46d6a7548af2f88","date":"2026-07-21T19:50:58.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)","message":"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)","ticketKeys":["O3-5822"],"pullRequests":[3496],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"23534665aa959b2921f11401aa2e275db61501f7","date":"2026-07-17T10:38:00.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"(chore) Include ngx-formentry in the OpenMRS dependency auto-update","message":"(chore) Include ngx-formentry in the OpenMRS dependency auto-update\n\nThe 4-hourly updater covers the framework, the React form engine lib,\nand the openmrs tooling, but not the Angular form engine, so the\nesm-form-entry-app lockfile resolution for @openmrs/ngx-formentry@next\nfroze at 20.0.1-pre.525 while the engine kept moving (the current next\nis pre.564, carrying the ICD-11 diagnosis code display, the endpoint\ndata source, and the remote-select centering fixes). Adding the package\nto the yarn up list lets the existing automation open the catch-up PR\nand keep the Angular engine current alongside its React peer.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e9b29360b21e0e0db589259b64f1ea4840f7f542","date":"2026-07-17T07:21:41.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) O3-5815: Return ICD-11 codes for diagnoses in the form-entry datasources (#3479)","message":"(feat) O3-5815: Return ICD-11 codes for diagnoses in the form-entry datasources (#3479)\n\nThe Angular form engine passes a diagnosis question's schema-level\ndatasource config (datasource.config, including conceptSourceUuid) to\nsearchOptions and resolveSelectedValue. The diagnoses datasource\npreviously ignored it, so no terminology code could be displayed next\nto a diagnosis.\n\n- findDiagnoses and resolveConcept accept an optional dataSourceOptions\n  argument. When it names a conceptSourceUuid, the concept search and\n  the selected-value lookup request conceptMappings in the rep and emit\n  a code field on the option, so the picker can render\n  \"{ICD11CODE} {Name}\" per the KNHTS convention.\n- The code comes from the concept's mapping to the configured source,\n  preferring SAME-AS mappings over other map types.\n- Concepts without a mapping to the source, and questions without the\n  config, behave exactly as before. Other datasources that share\n  mapConcept and resolveConcept are unchanged.\n\nCompanion to openmrs/openmrs-ngx-formentry#176, which renders the code\nfield.","ticketKeys":["O3-5815"],"pullRequests":[3479],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"b147fb5906f1c3df18f12e3c804daeea486813d2","date":"2026-06-22T11:11:48.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) Attach visit to visit note submissions (#3406)","message":"(fix) Attach visit to visit note submissions (#3406)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3406],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"64d3c9902168b1a43b08d5da09558e7da6288a0d","date":"2026-06-19T13:21:12.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","message":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3403],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6c28b2d62b57153a8a829e3507fea1c91cd54584","date":"2026-06-16T18:15:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Add e2e coverage for deleting program enrollments and editing visit notes (#3388)","message":"(test) Add e2e coverage for deleting program enrollments and editing visit notes (#3388)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3388],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"bd0350391135e8e0cb8ac61cabd0e3ce5256b28d","date":"2026-06-09T13:10:29.000Z","author":"sfortune","subject":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)","message":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)\n\nfix(O3-5709): use table-of-contents icon for Conditions to distinguish from task list\n\nThe Conditions item in the patient chart's left nav and the Task list in\nthe right rail both rendered omrs-icon-list-checked, falsely implying a\nsemantic link between a longitudinal clinical problem list and operational\naction items.\n\nSwitch Conditions to omrs-icon-table-of-contents, an already-registered,\nunclaimed glyph that reads as a list without the checklist connotation. This\nis an interim fix: the durable solution is a dedicated Conditions glyph in\nesm-styleguide (so ConditionsIcon stops aliasing ListCheckedIcon), tracked\nunder O3-5709.\n\nCo-authored-by: denniskigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-5709"],"pullRequests":[3359],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"3568fa685f2d33a17b6fb975b089ed4b0abb5cfe","date":"2026-05-17T21:37:59.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"fix: prevent escaped condition duplicate warnings","message":"fix: prevent escaped condition duplicate warnings","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"05cfbca7dbdd7488e868e1ffcb5d1ff0a00aac8b","date":"2026-04-30T10:50:10.000Z","author":"Skengmann","subject":"(fix) Correct casing of editCondition label (#3170)","message":"(fix) Correct casing of editCondition label (#3170)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3170],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"c7c10df4f1bec30712d71b2557e3222251827436","date":"2026-04-30T10:04:20.000Z","author":"Devarasetty Praneeth","subject":"(fix) O3-5444: Show inline warning when adding a duplicate condition (#3227)","message":"(fix) O3-5444: Show inline warning when adding a duplicate condition (#3227)","ticketKeys":["O3-5444"],"pullRequests":[3227],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart"],"revisions":["HEAD"],"messageTerms":["condition","diagnos","visit note"],"count":40},"coverageGaps":[],"truncated":["commits: answer byte cap reached; showing 22 of 40 found"]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b76189c9-712c-4cfa-8bd2-8a2b91f1ebd2","uuid":"8d8bad70-bbea-4504-97e3-893282492da2","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:11:08.942Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"d0f4b1bf5be04ad6f9c567635864b36de6ac36c3","date":"2026-10-07T13:20:03.000Z","author":"Veronica Mukuhi Muthee","subject":"(feat) O3-5823: Capture diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note (#3621)","message":"(feat) O3-5823: Capture diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note (#3621)","ticketKeys":["O3-5823"],"pullRequests":[3621],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"a0834be003ea69917f36dac8b4bccba52ba8a7a4","date":"2026-10-02T05:50:44.000Z","author":"chibongho","subject":"(fix) O3-6020: Make Visit Notes workspace accept an Encounter object for editing (#3719)","message":"(fix) O3-6020: Make Visit Notes workspace accept an Encounter object for editing (#3719)\n\n* (fix) O3-6020: Make Visit Notes workspace accept a Encounter object for editing\n\n* address feedback\n\n---------","ticketKeys":["O3-6020"],"pullRequests":[3719],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"108c48985b5e33905d025cb936a5657f45bb7a7a","date":"2026-09-24T20:50:01.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5998: Continue to the requested workspace after starting or selecting a visit (#3688)","message":"(fix) O3-5998: Continue to the requested workspace after starting or selecting a visit (#3688)\n\n* (fix) O3-5998: Continue to the requested workspace after starting or selecting a visit\n\nWhen a chart action needs a visit and the patient has none,\nuseStartVisitIfNeeded shows a visit prompt and waits for the user to start\nor pick a visit. Neither path continued to the workspace the user asked\nfor, so they had to click the action again.\n\nWith RDE off, the start visit dialog passes onVisitStarted into the\nstart-visit-workspace-form workspace, but the chart's wrapper for that\nworkspace never read it, so the promise never resolved. The wrapper now\naccepts onVisitStarted and calls it after it sets the visit context.\n\nWith RDE on, selecting a visit resolved the promise straight away. Setting\na new visit context makes the patient chart relaunch its workspace group\nonce the visit is refetched, and the relaunch closes every open window, so\nthe resumed workspace was closed before it rendered. The RDE-off path\nwould hit the same thing once the callback is wired up.\n\nThe patient chart store now records which visit the workspace group was\nlast launched with, and the chart sets it after each successful relaunch.\nuseStartVisitIfNeeded resolves true only once that matches the new visit\ncontext. Under RDE, closing the switcher after a selection no longer\nresolves false first.\n\n* Check that the visit note opens after starting a visit from the prompt\n\nThe visit context test already opens the visit note from the side rail\nwith no visit, starts a visit from the prompt, and waits for the Active\nVisit tag. It now also checks that the visit note form opens by itself\nand can still be written in once the chart has picked up the new visit,\nthen discards the note so the later delete visit steps start clean.\n\n* Resolve every pending visit prompt once the workspace group has the visit\n\nuseStartVisitIfNeeded kept a single pending resolver per hook instance, so\nif the same caller had two prompts comp","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-5998"],"pullRequests":[3688],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"4d9f19a2d629347559fe32b89899af6245c16e23","date":"2026-09-24T15:31:10.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5989: Keep a visit note saved when one of its images is rejected (#3670)","message":"(fix) O3-5989: Keep a visit note saved when one of its images is rejected (#3670)\n\nBy the time the images upload, the note and its diagnoses are already on\nthe server. A rejected image used to bubble into the catch handler, which\nshowed \"Error saving visit note\" and left the form open in create mode, so\nthe next Save and close posted a second note.\n\nUploads now run with Promise.allSettled. Every image the server accepts is\nsaved, the workspace closes as usual, and a warning snackbar names the\nimages that were rejected with the server's reason, pointing the user at\nthe note to add them again. A failure to save the note itself still shows\nthe error and keeps the form open.","ticketKeys":["O3-5989"],"pullRequests":[3670],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"52ad5642b88661b759f5e130f12e1d73a7fac66a","date":"2026-09-23T08:32:38.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)","message":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)\n\n* fix: O3-5990 Remove saved visit-note images safely\n\nConfirm removal of a saved image and void its observation through the obs endpoint. This preserves the encounter and diagnoses when the image is the only observation. Refresh attachment, note, and visit data after removal.\n\nExplain that removal takes effect immediately and discarding note edits will not restore the image. Cover cancel, success, and retry after failure. Verify that a blank note and its diagnosis survive removal of the sole image in the local browser and backend.\n\n* style: Put React first in image removal test imports\n\nMove the React import above the test utilities in the saved-image removal modal test.\n\n* fix: Save visit-note image removals with the form\n\nKeep image removals pending until Save and close, with Undo and Discard restoring the draft. Show a dimmed thumbnail and a separate Undo action for images marked for removal.\n\nRetry failed removals without repeating successful deletions, and avoid rewriting the note when only images change. Keep the visit-context header state stable during form updates.\n\n* fix: Refresh visit-note data once per save attempt\n\nRefresh after the removal batch and note save, including partial failures. Add coverage for saved diagnoses and successful and failed removal batches.\n\nSimplify the image markup, separate the error title from its explanation, and remove redundant footer styles.","ticketKeys":["O3-5990"],"pullRequests":[3684],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"96b812bb0206c034792895cacfad69dd3f37b44a","date":"2026-09-18T20:42:17.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5986: Show a visit note's saved images when editing it (#3668)","message":"(fix) O3-5986: Show a visit note's saved images when editing it (#3668)\n\nImages added to a visit note are uploaded with the note's encounter UUID, and the edit form loads and shows the attachments recorded on that encounter, read only. Only images added in the session live in form state, so a text-only edit uploads nothing. Attachment obs in the Visits page encounter expansion render as caption or file-name links that open a new read-only attachment-preview-modal, and the bytes URL helper moves to esm-patient-common-lib. Depends on openmrs/openmrs-esm-core#1887. Follow-ups: O3-5987, O3-5988, O3-5989, O3-5990.","ticketKeys":["O3-5986","O3-5987","O3-5988","O3-5989","O3-5990"],"pullRequests":[3668],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"385d75cc2bbcc2a6802ca4f96dde611072cd4dec","date":"2026-09-17T18:05:49.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls (#3663)","message":"(fix) Preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls (#3663)\n\n* fix: preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls\n\nTrack image additions and removals as form changes and read the current images for each upload callback so batches retain every file. Use labelled, contrasting remove buttons that do not submit the form. Cover create and edit workflows, batch uploads and removal.\n\n* fix: preserve image remove button contrast across interaction states\n\nSet explicit hover, focus and active colours so Carbon secondary button styles cannot hide the close icon. Remove the redundant button type, which Carbon already defaults to button.\n\n* fix: identify images in visit note removal labels\n\nUse the image description, filename or image number in each remove button's accessible name. Update the translation and tests to cover the fallbacks and select the intended image by name.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3663],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e8bf5eeaa08a65b4b8b1845e4ca1a224f3f90790","date":"2026-09-14T10:31:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)","message":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)\n\n* (fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form\n\nMake condition search results keyboard accessible with visible focus and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep the selected condition name in the input.\n\nUse Record condition for creation and Edit condition for editing. Update translations and cover keyboard navigation and workspace titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Remove unused conditions workspace title prop\n\nThe conditions form sets its edit title on Workspace2. Remove the unused launch prop and translation dependency, and update the action menu test to match.\n\n* Keep condition search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the search input when loading removes a focused result. Leave focus alone when the user has moved elsewhere, and test that keyboard input continues in the intended field.","ticketKeys":["O3-5969"],"pullRequests":[3646],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6961c3d13e74a69bc2ed96dc3fa5aa1cc4d86f25","date":"2026-09-11T21:11:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)","message":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)\n\n* (fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes\n\nMake diagnosis search results keyboard accessible and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep tablet row padding on the result button so its click target and focus outline fill the row.\n\nUse Add visit note and Edit visit note consistently in workspace titles and tablet headings. Update translations and cover the keyboard flow and titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Update visit context test for the add visit note title\n\nThe siderail opens the note workspace in creation mode. Expect Add visit note so the visit context test matches the renamed workspace title.\n\n* Keep diagnosis search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the corresponding diagnosis input when loading removes a focused result. Preserve focus when the user moves elsewhere, and cover continued typing in both diagnosis searches and the notes field.\n\n* Reduce spacing below open diagnosis results\n\nUse a smaller bottom margin while diagnosis results are visible. Keep the existing spacing when the list is closed. Verified desktop and tablet layouts and the visit-note E2E workflow.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3645],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"324603e9b2d62756416654585d2e6c1d1653fa14","date":"2026-09-01T20:29:42.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)","message":"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)\n\n* (fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label\n\nOn @carbon/react 1.x, the classic OverflowMenu pulls aria-label out of its props and applies it to the menu body (the ul with role menu), not to the trigger button. The trigger's accessible name comes from iconDescription, which defaults to 'Options'. Every overflow menu in this repo passed its label via aria-label, so screen readers announced a generic 'Options' for all of them.\n\nPass the label through iconDescription instead in the visit timeline, encounters table, orders and medications tables, and the allergies, conditions, procedures, programs, and vitals action menus. The conditions menu label was a hardcoded string, so it is now translated. Unit tests and e2e specs that located the triggers by the 'Options' name now use the real labels.\n\n* Keep aria-label on overflow menus so the popup stays named\n\nCarbon's classic OverflowMenu applies aria-label to the opened menu body (the ul with role menu), so dropping it left the popup without an accessible name. Keep aria-label alongside iconDescription so the trigger and the popup are both named. The encounters table test now asserts the popup's aria-label.\n\n* Disambiguate the delete confirmation locators in the e2e specs\n\nThe allergies, biometrics, and vitals trigger names now contain the word delete, so the modal confirmation locator getByRole('button', { name: /delete/i }) matched two elements and failed in strict mode. Target the modal's danger button instead, matching the existing conditions spec.\n\n* Cover the remaining overflow menu labels\n\nName the procedures, attachment preview, and clinical encounter list menus consistently. Remove the misplaced attachment menu item label and cover the accessible names in focused tests.\n\n* Update the procedures and attachments e2e locators for the new trigger names\n\nThe procedures and attachment preview triggers a","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3612],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"c6df9cf74c0b4e52986befd68a2fc9f19807bde6","date":"2026-08-18T14:03:07.000Z","author":"Ujjawal Prabhat","subject":"(fix) O3-5763: Let hosts handle encounter editing outside the chart (#3569)","message":"(fix) O3-5763: Let hosts handle encounter editing outside the chart (#3569)\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Let hosts handle encounter editing outside the chart\n\n* (chore) O3-5763: Cover both encounter edit paths in EncountersTable\n\n* (chore) O3-5763: Cover onEditEncounter pass-through and query by role\n\nAddresses review feedback on #3569:\n\n- Fold the edit-routing tests into the  block and\n  name each one for the path it covers (host callback vs the chart's own\n  workspaces).\n- Add cases for a form-backed visit note encounter and for the overflow\n  menu's edit item, not just the expanded row's button.\n- Assert VisitSummary threads onEditEncounter down to both the encounters\n  and completed forms tabs.\n- Query the overflow menu via  and the\n  expanded row's buttons at screen level, which drops the\n   disable from encounters-table.test.tsx.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","ticketKeys":["O3-5763"],"pullRequests":[3569],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"80db8ffc6ae52b7f708ed32aaa2f8a8b9abd4776","date":"2026-08-10T05:36:53.000Z","author":"Ujjawal Prabhat","subject":"(fix) O3-5763: Expose the visit notes form as a reusable workspace (#3509)","message":"(fix) O3-5763: Expose the visit notes form as a reusable workspace (#3509)\n\n* (fix) O3-5763: Expose the visit notes form as a reusable workspace\n\n* (chore) Move visit note form implementation into visit-notes-form.component.tsx\n\nAddresses review feedback on #3509. The shared form implementation lived in\nexported-visit-notes-form.workspace.tsx, which made the in-chart workspace\ndepend on the out-of-chart one and obscured the architecture.\n\nMove it to visit-notes-form.component.tsx and make both workspaces thin\nadapters over it, matching form entry, add drug order and the order basket.\nThe component body is unchanged apart from its props signature.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ujjawal Prabhat <ujjawal@Ujjawals-MacBook-Pro.local>\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>","ticketKeys":["O3-5763"],"pullRequests":[3509],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"1a2af778aa7f86ea2c1fc944e46d6a7548af2f88","date":"2026-07-21T19:50:58.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)","message":"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)","ticketKeys":["O3-5822"],"pullRequests":[3496],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"23534665aa959b2921f11401aa2e275db61501f7","date":"2026-07-17T10:38:00.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"(chore) Include ngx-formentry in the OpenMRS dependency auto-update","message":"(chore) Include ngx-formentry in the OpenMRS dependency auto-update\n\nThe 4-hourly updater covers the framework, the React form engine lib,\nand the openmrs tooling, but not the Angular form engine, so the\nesm-form-entry-app lockfile resolution for @openmrs/ngx-formentry@next\nfroze at 20.0.1-pre.525 while the engine kept moving (the current next\nis pre.564, carrying the ICD-11 diagnosis code display, the endpoint\ndata source, and the remote-select centering fixes). Adding the package\nto the yarn up list lets the existing automation open the catch-up PR\nand keep the Angular engine current alongside its React peer.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e9b29360b21e0e0db589259b64f1ea4840f7f542","date":"2026-07-17T07:21:41.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) O3-5815: Return ICD-11 codes for diagnoses in the form-entry datasources (#3479)","message":"(feat) O3-5815: Return ICD-11 codes for diagnoses in the form-entry datasources (#3479)\n\nThe Angular form engine passes a diagnosis question's schema-level\ndatasource config (datasource.config, including conceptSourceUuid) to\nsearchOptions and resolveSelectedValue. The diagnoses datasource\npreviously ignored it, so no terminology code could be displayed next\nto a diagnosis.\n\n- findDiagnoses and resolveConcept accept an optional dataSourceOptions\n  argument. When it names a conceptSourceUuid, the concept search and\n  the selected-value lookup request conceptMappings in the rep and emit\n  a code field on the option, so the picker can render\n  \"{ICD11CODE} {Name}\" per the KNHTS convention.\n- The code comes from the concept's mapping to the configured source,\n  preferring SAME-AS mappings over other map types.\n- Concepts without a mapping to the source, and questions without the\n  config, behave exactly as before. Other datasources that share\n  mapConcept and resolveConcept are unchanged.\n\nCompanion to openmrs/openmrs-ngx-formentry#176, which renders the code\nfield.","ticketKeys":["O3-5815"],"pullRequests":[3479],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"b147fb5906f1c3df18f12e3c804daeea486813d2","date":"2026-06-22T11:11:48.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) Attach visit to visit note submissions (#3406)","message":"(fix) Attach visit to visit note submissions (#3406)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3406],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"64d3c9902168b1a43b08d5da09558e7da6288a0d","date":"2026-06-19T13:21:12.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","message":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3403],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6c28b2d62b57153a8a829e3507fea1c91cd54584","date":"2026-06-16T18:15:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Add e2e coverage for deleting program enrollments and editing visit notes (#3388)","message":"(test) Add e2e coverage for deleting program enrollments and editing visit notes (#3388)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3388],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"bd0350391135e8e0cb8ac61cabd0e3ce5256b28d","date":"2026-06-09T13:10:29.000Z","author":"sfortune","subject":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)","message":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)\n\nfix(O3-5709): use table-of-contents icon for Conditions to distinguish from task list\n\nThe Conditions item in the patient chart's left nav and the Task list in\nthe right rail both rendered omrs-icon-list-checked, falsely implying a\nsemantic link between a longitudinal clinical problem list and operational\naction items.\n\nSwitch Conditions to omrs-icon-table-of-contents, an already-registered,\nunclaimed glyph that reads as a list without the checklist connotation. This\nis an interim fix: the durable solution is a dedicated Conditions glyph in\nesm-styleguide (so ConditionsIcon stops aliasing ListCheckedIcon), tracked\nunder O3-5709.\n\nCo-authored-by: denniskigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-5709"],"pullRequests":[3359],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"3568fa685f2d33a17b6fb975b089ed4b0abb5cfe","date":"2026-05-17T21:37:59.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"fix: prevent escaped condition duplicate warnings","message":"fix: prevent escaped condition duplicate warnings","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"05cfbca7dbdd7488e868e1ffcb5d1ff0a00aac8b","date":"2026-04-30T10:50:10.000Z","author":"Skengmann","subject":"(fix) Correct casing of editCondition label (#3170)","message":"(fix) Correct casing of editCondition label (#3170)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3170],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"c7c10df4f1bec30712d71b2557e3222251827436","date":"2026-04-30T10:04:20.000Z","author":"Devarasetty Praneeth","subject":"(fix) O3-5444: Show inline warning when adding a duplicate condition (#3227)","message":"(fix) O3-5444: Show inline warning when adding a duplicate condition (#3227)","ticketKeys":["O3-5444"],"pullRequests":[3227],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":[