{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgacCuGbAzSSDMVaKGeFz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LvhXSTcyGn1Zu2a5EbfKp4","name":"mcp__falkon__search_commits","input":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart"],"messageTerms":["problem list","problem-list","reload","refresh","SWR","invalidate","visit note conditions"],"count":30},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11420,"cache_read_input_tokens":29927,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11420},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b76189c9-712c-4cfa-8bd2-8a2b91f1ebd2","uuid":"5934587c-6652-4080-b917-0edc63907964","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:11:12.510Z","request_id":"req_011CgacCtzENFEMXT56ZNPKE","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LvhXSTcyGn1Zu2a5EbfKp4":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart"],"messageTerms":["problem list","problem-list","reload","refresh","SWR","invalidate","visit note conditions"],"count":30}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LvhXSTcyGn1Zu2a5EbfKp4","display_name":"Search Commits","server_display_name":"falkon-mcp-server","tool_name":"search_commits"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LvhXSTcyGn1Zu2a5EbfKp4","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"4c50ae55de4b35367c7edb12f1e6b1a7b8388b42","date":"2026-09-30T17:04:59.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Revalidate the visit context in invalidateVisitByUuid (#3720)","message":"(fix) Revalidate the visit context in invalidateVisitByUuid (#3720)\n\n* (fix) Revalidate the visit context in invalidateVisitByUuid\n\ninvalidateVisitByUuid passed a RegExp to SWR's mutate. SWR only treats a\nfunction as a key filter, so it serialized the RegExp as a single literal\nkey that matched no cache entry, and the call did nothing.\n\nStarting or editing a visit, switching the visit context, and restoring a\ndeleted visit all store this helper as the patient chart's\nmutateVisitContext. After any of those, later mutateVisitContext calls\n(order basket, form entry, deleting an encounter, the vitals launcher)\nnever refetched the visit until the page was reloaded. The medications\nand orders tables also call it directly.\n\nUse a key filter function instead, like the other helpers in\nrevalidation-utils.ts, and add a test for it.\n\n* Pass invalidateVisitByUuid as a function in the orders table\n\nOrderBasketItemActions called invalidateVisitByUuid while building its\nworkspace group props instead of wrapping it in a function. That left\nmutateVisitContext undefined for order basket workspaces launched from\nthe orders table. Now that invalidateVisitByUuid actually revalidates,\nit also refetched the visit context every time an order row from that\nvisit rendered.\n\n* Handle orders without a visit and test the order basket refresh\n\nUse optional chaining on the order's encounter visit, like the\nmedications table, so mutateVisitContext doesn't throw for an order whose\nencounter has no visit. Encounter.visit is optional in the framework\ntypes and nullable in openmrs-core.\n\nAdd a test that cancelling an order launches the order basket with a\nmutateVisitContext function, since it was undefined before.\n\n* Skip invalidateVisitByUuid when there's no visit UUID\n\nThe medications and orders tables pass encounter.visit?.uuid, so the\nvisit UUID can be undefined. Reflect that in the type and return early\ninstead of scanning the cache for /visit/undefined.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3720],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"715ec982cb5008f64cf590e3335001b4de19843e","date":"2026-09-29T19:25:43.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry (#3692)","message":"(fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry (#3692)\n\n* (fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry\n\nSave lab results and discontinue the test order in a single encounter\nrequest, then mark the order as fulfilled. The backend saves inline\norders inside the same transaction as the obs, so a failed discontinue\nno longer leaves the results saved behind it.\n\nPreviously the results, the discontinue and the fulfiller update were\nthree separate requests. If a later one failed, the results were already\nsaved, the order was not COMPLETED, and the form stayed in create mode.\nRetrying posted the obs to the encounter again. If the fulfiller update\nwas the one that failed, every retry added another copy and then failed\non the discontinue, because the backend rejects stopping an order twice.\n\nWhen an order already has saved results but is not COMPLETED, the form\nnow fills in the saved values and saving updates those obs. It then\ndiscontinues the order only if it is still active and marks it as\nfulfilled. A failed save refetches the saved results so the next attempt\nsees them.\n\n* Check for saved results when the user saves\n\nDecide whether to create or update results from a fresh fetch of the\norder's encounter at submit time, instead of the results the form loaded\nearlier. After a failed attempt, the form refetches its results in the\nbackground, and Save is available again before that refetch finishes.\nA quick retry in that window used to take the create path again. If the\nfetch fails, nothing is saved.\n\n* Keep the user's edits when saved results load\n\nOnly fill in saved result values for fields the user hasn't changed.\nAfter a failed save, the form refetches the saved results, and if the\nuser corrected a value while that was in flight, the refetched value\nreplaced their correction.\n\n* test: verify lab result edits are saved after delayed refresh\n\nExtend the delayed-results regression test through Save and close. Check that the corrected value is submitted, the workspa","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-6004"],"pullRequests":[3692],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"47ac43e14be3f538904a7c94e509e65624dae35e","date":"2026-09-28T15:35:43.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Pass a string subtitle to the general order form's error snackbar (#3700)","message":"(fix) Pass a string subtitle to the general order form's error snackbar (#3700)\n\nWhen saving a revised general order failed, the form passed the raw\nOpenmrsFetchError to showSnackbar as the subtitle. React can't render an\nError object as a child, so the snackbar host threw and unmounted, and no\nlater snackbars showed until the page was reloaded.\n\nShow the backend's error message instead, falling back to the error's own\nmessage. This matches how the order basket tile and the lab results form\nin this package read order errors. Adds a test for the failed-save path.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3700],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"52ad5642b88661b759f5e130f12e1d73a7fac66a","date":"2026-09-23T08:32:38.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)","message":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)\n\n* fix: O3-5990 Remove saved visit-note images safely\n\nConfirm removal of a saved image and void its observation through the obs endpoint. This preserves the encounter and diagnoses when the image is the only observation. Refresh attachment, note, and visit data after removal.\n\nExplain that removal takes effect immediately and discarding note edits will not restore the image. Cover cancel, success, and retry after failure. Verify that a blank note and its diagnosis survive removal of the sole image in the local browser and backend.\n\n* style: Put React first in image removal test imports\n\nMove the React import above the test utilities in the saved-image removal modal test.\n\n* fix: Save visit-note image removals with the form\n\nKeep image removals pending until Save and close, with Undo and Discard restoring the draft. Show a dimmed thumbnail and a separate Undo action for images marked for removal.\n\nRetry failed removals without repeating successful deletions, and avoid rewriting the note when only images change. Keep the visit-context header state stable during form updates.\n\n* fix: Refresh visit-note data once per save attempt\n\nRefresh after the removal batch and note save, including partial failures. Add coverage for saved diagnoses and successful and failed removal batches.\n\nSimplify the image markup, separate the error title from its explanation, and remove redundant footer styles.","ticketKeys":["O3-5990"],"pullRequests":[3684],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"83bda4a0d37d5bf6aacce9d46e47a4ceb228b3d6","date":"2026-09-19T16:33:14.000Z","author":"Ian","subject":"(chore) Upgrade to version 2.5.1 of SWR (#3675)","message":"(chore) Upgrade to version 2.5.1 of SWR (#3675)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3675],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e8bf5eeaa08a65b4b8b1845e4ca1a224f3f90790","date":"2026-09-14T10:31:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)","message":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)\n\n* (fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form\n\nMake condition search results keyboard accessible with visible focus and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep the selected condition name in the input.\n\nUse Record condition for creation and Edit condition for editing. Update translations and cover keyboard navigation and workspace titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Remove unused conditions workspace title prop\n\nThe conditions form sets its edit title on Workspace2. Remove the unused launch prop and translation dependency, and update the action menu test to match.\n\n* Keep condition search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the search input when loading removes a focused result. Leave focus alone when the user has moved elsewhere, and test that keyboard input continues in the intended field.","ticketKeys":["O3-5969"],"pullRequests":[3646],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6961c3d13e74a69bc2ed96dc3fa5aa1cc4d86f25","date":"2026-09-11T21:11:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)","message":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)\n\n* (fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes\n\nMake diagnosis search results keyboard accessible and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep tablet row padding on the result button so its click target and focus outline fill the row.\n\nUse Add visit note and Edit visit note consistently in workspace titles and tablet headings. Update translations and cover the keyboard flow and titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Update visit context test for the add visit note title\n\nThe siderail opens the note workspace in creation mode. Expect Add visit note so the visit context test matches the renamed workspace title.\n\n* Keep diagnosis search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the corresponding diagnosis input when loading removes a focused result. Preserve focus when the user moves elsewhere, and cover continued typing in both diagnosis searches and the notes field.\n\n* Reduce spacing below open diagnosis results\n\nUse a smaller bottom margin while diagnosis results are visible. Keep the existing spacing when the list is closed. Verified desktop and tablet layouts and the visit-note E2E workflow.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3645],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"f4b9490ba78fe5ee0be814d8b88c9cb67c183799","date":"2026-08-20T17:22:59.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Correct data handling defects in the generic obs widgets (#3587)","message":"(fix) Correct data handling defects in the generic obs widgets (#3587)\n\n* (fix) Correct data handling defects in the generic obs widgets\n\nThe editable horizontal obs table discarded a typed value of 0 because\nthe save guard treated it as empty input. A numeric zero now saves;\nonly genuinely empty input bails.\n\nAn observation without an encounter crashed every widget built on\nuseObs, which dereferenced the FHIR encounter reference unguarded.\nObservation.encounter is optional in FHIR. Encounter-less obs now map\nwith no encounter and render as their own rows in the obs table. The\nmapping also no longer mutates the FHIR resources held in the SWR\ncache.\n\nA configured decimalPlaces of 0 was ignored because both tables tested\ndecimalPlaces > 0 and fell back to two decimal places. An explicit 0\nnow rounds to whole numbers.\n\nNumeric columns sorted incorrectly because integer values are stored as\nnumbers while fractional values are toFixed strings, and the comparator\ncompared them as strings. Numeric columns now compare numeric values.\n\n* (fix) Guard encounter type sorting against obs without an encounter\n\nEncounter-less obs now render as their own rows, so the encounter cell\ncan be undefined. Sorting the encounter type column called localeCompare\non it directly and crashed the widget. Coalesce to an empty string and\ncover it with a regression test that clicks the header.\n\n* (fix) Rename _validator to _validators in the obs widget config schemas\n\nThe config system only reads the plural key, so the inRange(0, 10)\nchecks on decimalPlaces never ran. With this rename, an out-of-range\ndecimalPlaces gets a validation error at startup instead of passing\nthrough silently.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3587],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"64d3c9902168b1a43b08d5da09558e7da6288a0d","date":"2026-06-19T13:21:12.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","message":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3403],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"bd0350391135e8e0cb8ac61cabd0e3ce5256b28d","date":"2026-06-09T13:10:29.000Z","author":"sfortune","subject":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)","message":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)\n\nfix(O3-5709): use table-of-contents icon for Conditions to distinguish from task list\n\nThe Conditions item in the patient chart's left nav and the Task list in\nthe right rail both rendered omrs-icon-list-checked, falsely implying a\nsemantic link between a longitudinal clinical problem list and operational\naction items.\n\nSwitch Conditions to omrs-icon-table-of-contents, an already-registered,\nunclaimed glyph that reads as a list without the checklist connotation. This\nis an interim fix: the durable solution is a dedicated Conditions glyph in\nesm-styleguide (so ConditionsIcon stops aliasing ListCheckedIcon), tracked\nunder O3-5709.\n\nCo-authored-by: denniskigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-5709"],"pullRequests":[3359],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e8a91dc03fb49a124935db66973019874361c307","date":"2026-05-15T18:35:22.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Port task-list tests from openmrs-esm-task-list#9 (#3303)","message":"(test) Port task-list tests from openmrs-esm-task-list#9 (#3303)\n\n* (test) Port task-list tests from openmrs-esm-task-list#9\n\nSalvages the test work from @pirupius's PR\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-task-list#9 before the standalone repo is archived\n(its source was forked into packages/esm-patient-task-list-app).\n\nUnit tests\n----------\nAdds the gap-filling test cases from pirupius's three test files to the\nexisting patient-chart equivalents. Each new test was rewritten in\nvitest style and adapted to patient-chart's evolved components; tests\nthat duplicate already-covered behaviour were skipped.\n\ndelete-task.modal.test.tsx (+3)\n  - mutates the SWR cache after successful deletion\n  - shows a loading state while deletion is in progress\n  - disables the Delete button while deletion is in progress\n\n  Required mocking `useSWRConfig` at module level so the mutate call\n  the component issues against `taskListSWRKey(patientUuid)` is\n  observable.\n\ntask-list-view.test.tsx (+5)\n  - falls back to the assignee uuid when display is missing\n  - does not render a priority tag when the task has no priority\n  - does not show the overdue tag for tasks due today (boundary case\n    for the `dueDateOnly < nowDateOnly` comparison in the component)\n  - unchecks a completed task when its checkbox is toggled\n\n  Plus one already-covered case I left in pirupius's file out of scope.\n\ntask-list.workspace.test.tsx (+4)\n  - renders the add-task-form (not edit-task-form) in create mode\n  - returns to list when AddTaskForm calls onClose from the form view\n  - returns to list when TaskDetailsView calls onBack\n  - returns to details when the edit form calls onClose (covers\n    handleEditComplete which differs from the workspace back button)\n\n  Existing tests already cover the workspace-header back button paths\n  for both form and details views.\n\n64 vitest tests pass (was 50). `yarn typescript` clean.\n\nE2E spec\n--------\nPorts pirupius's `e2e/specs/task-list.spec.ts` (6 tests) plus the\ntask-list-specific helpers,","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3303],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"0a600e002315bccbb808b2ff5a2cbe05d2a6f8a4","date":"2026-03-03T21:10:36.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Refresh queue table UI when deleting or restoring a visit (#3076)","message":"(fix) Refresh queue table UI when deleting or restoring a visit (#3076)\n\nThe backend queue module already voids/unvoids queue entries when a visit\nis voided/restored via VisitWithQueueEntriesSaveHandler, but the frontend\nqueue table didn't know to refetch. Dispatch the 'queue-entry-updated'\nevent on both delete and restore so the service queues UI stays in sync.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3076],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"efc6d8f527acc021de816ff8f85d7015a0b48137","date":"2026-02-24T14:29:38.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve mark deceased/alive workflows (#3050)","message":"(fix) Improve mark deceased/alive workflows (#3050)\n\n* (fix) Improve mark deceased/alive workflows\n\nReplace window.location.reload() with targeted SWR cache invalidation in both the mark-deceased form and mark-alive modal. After toggling death status, the patient data, current visit, and visit/encounter caches are revalidated so the UI updates reactively without a full page reload.\n\nAlso adds death date validation against the patient's date of birth: the date picker now sets minDate to the patient's birth date, and a Zod refine rejects death dates before DOB. The backend already has this check in PersonValidator, but the frontend was not enforcing it, allowing the user to submit and get a generic error toast.\n\nUpdates the warning text from \"will end any active visits\" to \"updates this patient's death information\" since the current /person endpoint does not actually close visits.\n\n* Update markDeceasedWarning translation to match component","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3050],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"ebb3f1156a112c4e6eae3a1c2917e77fe5aa8acd","date":"2026-02-24T13:43:57.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5447: Use encounter's own visit context when editing (#3056)","message":"(fix) O3-5447: Use encounter's own visit context when editing (#3056)\n\nWhen editing an encounter from a past (closed) visit, the form entry\ncomponent was using the active visit's context instead of the\nencounter's actual visit. This caused the backend to reject edits with\n\"The encounter datetime should be between the visit start and stop\ndates.\"\n\nThis commit fixes the issue by fetching the encounter's visit via a\nlightweight SWR call when `encounterUuid` is present, and gate form\nrendering until the data resolves. For visitless encounters, the visit\ncontext is correctly left null rather than falling back to the active visit.","ticketKeys":["O3-5447"],"pullRequests":[3056],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"ee157646a8d93be7ced49d8a0eaa341ed67321d3","date":"2026-02-06T22:50:28.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Disable test results refresh button while revalidation is in-flight","message":"(fix) Disable test results refresh button while revalidation is in-flight\n\nPrevent duplicate refresh requests by tracking the refresh state and\ndisabling the button until all SWR revalidations have settled.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"11fef2c97a225178fd0051c62fae6523432f2128","date":"2026-02-05T20:24:05.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Use targeted SWR cache invalidation for test results refresh (#2998)","message":"(fix) Use targeted SWR cache invalidation for test results refresh (#2998)\n\nReplace `window.location.reload()` with SWR cache mutation to refresh\ntest results data without a full page reload. Iterates over cache keys\ndirectly rather than using a filter function, since SWR's `mutate()`\nwith a filter explicitly skips `$inf$`-prefixed keys from\n`useSWRInfinite` hooks.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2998],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"21b4b98ddcea58e5ba3ec71fa8f974c47359bd41","date":"2026-02-05T17:37:27.000Z","author":"Souravjyoti Dutta","subject":"(fix) O3-5319: Refresh test results viewer after saving lab results (#2983)","message":"(fix) O3-5319: Refresh test results viewer after saving lab results (#2983)","ticketKeys":["O3-5319"],"pullRequests":[2983],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"03d6a5b9a61e3bc255cfa1281dc9d488f1ffd469","date":"2026-02-03T09:11:56.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Fix delete visit modal receiving undefined visit prop (#2985)","message":"(fix) Fix delete visit modal receiving undefined visit prop (#2985)\n\n* (fix) Fix delete visit modal receiving undefined visit prop\n\nThe delete visit modal expected an `activeVisit` prop but callers passed\nvisit, causing the modal to receive `undefined`. This rename also\nremoves the redundant `mutateActiveVisit` callback, since\n`invalidateVisitAndEncounterData` already handles SWR revalidation.\n\nThis change also adds unit tests for the delete visit action item component\nand an e2e test for deleting a visit from the visit history table.\n\n* Use dynamic birthdate in e2e test patient fixture\n\nUse a dynamically computed birthdate (5 years ago) instead of a\nhardcoded '2020-2-1' date. The hardcoded date caused test failures\nas time passed because age-dependent reference ranges and UI logic\nwould shift relative to the fixed date.\n\n* Make patient birthdate deterministic without timezone conversion\n\nBuild the birthdate as a YYYY-MM-DD string based on the current year.\nAvoids UTC conversion drift from toISOString in e2e tests.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2985],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart"],"revisions":["HEAD"],"messageTerms":["problem list","problem-list","reload","refresh","SWR","invalidate","visit note conditions"],"count":30},"coverageGaps":[],"truncated":["commits: answer byte cap reached; showing 18 of 30 found"]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b76189c9-712c-4cfa-8bd2-8a2b91f1ebd2","uuid":"a698425e-2f87-4920-bac0-1772bbb28bd8","timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:11:12.639Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"4c50ae55de4b35367c7edb12f1e6b1a7b8388b42","date":"2026-09-30T17:04:59.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Revalidate the visit context in invalidateVisitByUuid (#3720)","message":"(fix) Revalidate the visit context in invalidateVisitByUuid (#3720)\n\n* (fix) Revalidate the visit context in invalidateVisitByUuid\n\ninvalidateVisitByUuid passed a RegExp to SWR's mutate. SWR only treats a\nfunction as a key filter, so it serialized the RegExp as a single literal\nkey that matched no cache entry, and the call did nothing.\n\nStarting or editing a visit, switching the visit context, and restoring a\ndeleted visit all store this helper as the patient chart's\nmutateVisitContext. After any of those, later mutateVisitContext calls\n(order basket, form entry, deleting an encounter, the vitals launcher)\nnever refetched the visit until the page was reloaded. The medications\nand orders tables also call it directly.\n\nUse a key filter function instead, like the other helpers in\nrevalidation-utils.ts, and add a test for it.\n\n* Pass invalidateVisitByUuid as a function in the orders table\n\nOrderBasketItemActions called invalidateVisitByUuid while building its\nworkspace group props instead of wrapping it in a function. That left\nmutateVisitContext undefined for order basket workspaces launched from\nthe orders table. Now that invalidateVisitByUuid actually revalidates,\nit also refetched the visit context every time an order row from that\nvisit rendered.\n\n* Handle orders without a visit and test the order basket refresh\n\nUse optional chaining on the order's encounter visit, like the\nmedications table, so mutateVisitContext doesn't throw for an order whose\nencounter has no visit. Encounter.visit is optional in the framework\ntypes and nullable in openmrs-core.\n\nAdd a test that cancelling an order launches the order basket with a\nmutateVisitContext function, since it was undefined before.\n\n* Skip invalidateVisitByUuid when there's no visit UUID\n\nThe medications and orders tables pass encounter.visit?.uuid, so the\nvisit UUID can be undefined. Reflect that in the type and return early\ninstead of scanning the cache for /visit/undefined.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3720],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"715ec982cb5008f64cf590e3335001b4de19843e","date":"2026-09-29T19:25:43.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry (#3692)","message":"(fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry (#3692)\n\n* (fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry\n\nSave lab results and discontinue the test order in a single encounter\nrequest, then mark the order as fulfilled. The backend saves inline\norders inside the same transaction as the obs, so a failed discontinue\nno longer leaves the results saved behind it.\n\nPreviously the results, the discontinue and the fulfiller update were\nthree separate requests. If a later one failed, the results were already\nsaved, the order was not COMPLETED, and the form stayed in create mode.\nRetrying posted the obs to the encounter again. If the fulfiller update\nwas the one that failed, every retry added another copy and then failed\non the discontinue, because the backend rejects stopping an order twice.\n\nWhen an order already has saved results but is not COMPLETED, the form\nnow fills in the saved values and saving updates those obs. It then\ndiscontinues the order only if it is still active and marks it as\nfulfilled. A failed save refetches the saved results so the next attempt\nsees them.\n\n* Check for saved results when the user saves\n\nDecide whether to create or update results from a fresh fetch of the\norder's encounter at submit time, instead of the results the form loaded\nearlier. After a failed attempt, the form refetches its results in the\nbackground, and Save is available again before that refetch finishes.\nA quick retry in that window used to take the create path again. If the\nfetch fails, nothing is saved.\n\n* Keep the user's edits when saved results load\n\nOnly fill in saved result values for fields the user hasn't changed.\nAfter a failed save, the form refetches the saved results, and if the\nuser corrected a value while that was in flight, the refetched value\nreplaced their correction.\n\n* test: verify lab result edits are saved after delayed refresh\n\nExtend the delayed-results regression test through Save and close. Check that the corrected value is submitted, the workspa","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-6004"],"pullRequests":[3692],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"47ac43e14be3f538904a7c94e509e65624dae35e","date":"2026-09-28T15:35:43.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Pass a string subtitle to the general order form's error snackbar (#3700)","message":"(fix) Pass a string subtitle to the general order form's error snackbar (#3700)\n\nWhen saving a revised general order failed, the form passed the raw\nOpenmrsFetchError to showSnackbar as the subtitle. React can't render an\nError object as a child, so the snackbar host threw and unmounted, and no\nlater snackbars showed until the page was reloaded.\n\nShow the backend's error message instead, falling back to the error's own\nmessage. This matches how the order basket tile and the lab results form\nin this package read order errors. Adds a test for the failed-save path.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3700],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"52ad5642b88661b759f5e130f12e1d73a7fac66a","date":"2026-09-23T08:32:38.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)","message":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)\n\n* fix: O3-5990 Remove saved visit-note images safely\n\nConfirm removal of a saved image and void its observation through the obs endpoint. This preserves the encounter and diagnoses when the image is the only observation. Refresh attachment, note, and visit data after removal.\n\nExplain that removal takes effect immediately and discarding note edits will not restore the image. Cover cancel, success, and retry after failure. Verify that a blank note and its diagnosis survive removal of the sole image in the local browser and backend.\n\n* style: Put React first in image removal test imports\n\nMove the React import above the test utilities in the saved-image removal modal test.\n\n* fix: Save visit-note image removals with the form\n\nKeep image removals pending until Save and close, with Undo and Discard restoring the draft. Show a dimmed thumbnail and a separate Undo action for images marked for removal.\n\nRetry failed removals without repeating successful deletions, and avoid rewriting the note when only images change. Keep the visit-context header state stable during form updates.\n\n* fix: Refresh visit-note data once per save attempt\n\nRefresh after the removal batch and note save, including partial failures. Add coverage for saved diagnoses and successful and failed removal batches.\n\nSimplify the image markup, separate the error title from its explanation, and remove redundant footer styles.","ticketKeys":["O3-5990"],"pullRequests":[3684],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"83bda4a0d37d5bf6aacce9d46e47a4ceb228b3d6","date":"2026-09-19T16:33:14.000Z","author":"Ian","subject":"(chore) Upgrade to version 2.5.1 of SWR (#3675)","message":"(chore) Upgrade to version 2.5.1 of SWR (#3675)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3675],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e8bf5eeaa08a65b4b8b1845e4ca1a224f3f90790","date":"2026-09-14T10:31:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)","message":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)\n\n* (fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form\n\nMake condition search results keyboard accessible with visible focus and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep the selected condition name in the input.\n\nUse Record condition for creation and Edit condition for editing. Update translations and cover keyboard navigation and workspace titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Remove unused conditions workspace title prop\n\nThe conditions form sets its edit title on Workspace2. Remove the unused launch prop and translation dependency, and update the action menu test to match.\n\n* Keep condition search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the search input when loading removes a focused result. Leave focus alone when the user has moved elsewhere, and test that keyboard input continues in the intended field.","ticketKeys":["O3-5969"],"pullRequests":[3646],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6961c3d13e74a69bc2ed96dc3fa5aa1cc4d86f25","date":"2026-09-11T21:11:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)","message":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)\n\n* (fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes\n\nMake diagnosis search results keyboard accessible and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep tablet row padding on the result button so its click target and focus outline fill the row.\n\nUse Add visit note and Edit visit note consistently in workspace titles and tablet headings. Update translations and cover the keyboard flow and titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Update visit context test for the add visit note title\n\nThe siderail opens the note workspace in creation mode. Expect Add visit note so the visit context test matches the renamed workspace title.\n\n* Keep diagnosis search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the corresponding diagnosis input when loading removes a focused result. Preserve focus when the user moves elsewhere, and cover continued typing in both diagnosis searches and the notes field.\n\n* Reduce spacing below open diagnosis results\n\nUse a smaller bottom margin while diagnosis results are visible. Keep the existing spacing when the list is closed. Verified desktop and tablet layouts and the visit-note E2E workflow.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3645],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"f4b9490ba78fe5ee0be814d8b88c9cb67c183799","date":"2026-08-20T17:22:59.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Correct data handling defects in the generic obs widgets (#3587)","message":"(fix) Correct data handling defects in the generic obs widgets (#3587)\n\n* (fix) Correct data handling defects in the generic obs widgets\n\nThe editable horizontal obs table discarded a typed value of 0 because\nthe save guard treated it as empty input. A numeric zero now saves;\nonly genuinely empty input bails.\n\nAn observation without an encounter crashed every widget built on\nuseObs, which dereferenced the FHIR encounter reference unguarded.\nObservation.encounter is optional in FHIR. Encounter-less obs now map\nwith no encounter and render as their own rows in the obs table. The\nmapping also no longer mutates the FHIR resources held in the SWR\ncache.\n\nA configured decimalPlaces of 0 was ignored because both tables tested\ndecimalPlaces > 0 and fell back to two decimal places. An explicit 0\nnow rounds to whole numbers.\n\nNumeric columns sorted incorrectly because integer values are stored as\nnumbers while fractional values are toFixed strings, and the comparator\ncompared them as strings. Numeric columns now compare numeric values.\n\n* (fix) Guard encounter type sorting against obs without an encounter\n\nEncounter-less obs now render as their own rows, so the encounter cell\ncan be undefined. Sorting the encounter type column called localeCompare\non it directly and crashed the widget. Coalesce to an empty string and\ncover it with a regression test that clicks the header.\n\n* (fix) Rename _validator to _validators in the obs widget config schemas\n\nThe config system only reads the plural key, so the inRange(0, 10)\nchecks on decimalPlaces never ran. With this rename, an out-of-range\ndecimalPlaces gets a validation error at startup instead of passing\nthrough silently.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3587],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"64d3c9902168b1a43b08d5da09558e7da6288a0d","date":"2026-06-19T13:21:12.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","message":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3403],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"bd0350391135e8e0cb8ac61cabd0e3ce5256b28d","date":"2026-06-09T13:10:29.000Z","author":"sfortune","subject":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)","message":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)\n\nfix(O3-5709): use table-of-contents icon for Conditions to distinguish from task list\n\nThe Conditions item in the patient chart's left nav and the Task list in\nthe right rail both rendered omrs-icon-list-checked, falsely implying a\nsemantic link between a longitudinal clinical problem list and operational\naction items.\n\nSwitch Conditions to omrs-icon-table-of-contents, an already-registered,\nunclaimed glyph that reads as a list without the checklist connotation. This\nis an interim fix: the durable solution is a dedicated Conditions glyph in\nesm-styleguide (so ConditionsIcon stops aliasing ListCheckedIcon), tracked\nunder O3-5709.\n\nCo-authored-by: denniskigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-5709"],"pullRequests":[3359],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e8a91dc03fb49a124935db66973019874361c307","date":"2026-05-15T18:35:22.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Port task-list tests from openmrs-esm-task-list#9 (#3303)","message":"(test) Port task-list tests from openmrs-esm-task-list#9 (#3303)\n\n* (test) Port task-list tests from openmrs-esm-task-list#9\n\nSalvages the test work from @pirupius's PR\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-task-list#9 before the standalone repo is archived\n(its source was forked into packages/esm-patient-task-list-app).\n\nUnit tests\n----------\nAdds the gap-filling test cases from pirupius's three test files to the\nexisting patient-chart equivalents. Each new test was rewritten in\nvitest style and adapted to patient-chart's evolved components; tests\nthat duplicate already-covered behaviour were skipped.\n\ndelete-task.modal.test.tsx (+3)\n  - mutates the SWR cache after successful deletion\n  - shows a loading state while deletion is in progress\n  - disables the Delete button while deletion is in progress\n\n  Required mocking `useSWRConfig` at module level so the mutate call\n  the component issues against `taskListSWRKey(patientUuid)` is\n  observable.\n\ntask-list-view.test.tsx (+5)\n  - falls back to the assignee uuid when display is missing\n  - does not render a priority tag when the task has no priority\n  - does not show the overdue tag for tasks due today (boundary case\n    for the `dueDateOnly < nowDateOnly` comparison in the component)\n  - unchecks a completed task when its checkbox is toggled\n\n  Plus one already-covered case I left in pirupius's file out of scope.\n\ntask-list.workspace.test.tsx (+4)\n  - renders the add-task-form (not edit-task-form) in create mode\n  - returns to list when AddTaskForm calls onClose from the form view\n  - returns to list when TaskDetailsView calls onBack\n  - returns to details when the edit form calls onClose (covers\n    handleEditComplete which differs from the workspace back button)\n\n  Existing tests already cover the workspace-header back button paths\n  for both form and details views.\n\n64 vitest tests pass (was 50). `yarn typescript` clean.\n\nE2E spec\n--------\nPorts pirupius's `e2e/specs/task-list.spec.ts` (6 tests) plus the\ntask-list-specific helpers,","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3303],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"0a600e002315bccbb808b2ff5a2cbe05d2a6f8a4","date":"2026-03-03T21:10:36.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Refresh queue table UI when deleting or restoring a visit (#3076)","message":"(fix) Refresh queue table UI when deleting or restoring a visit (#3076)\n\nThe backend queue module already voids/unvoids queue entries when a visit\nis voided/restored via VisitWithQueueEntriesSaveHandler, but the frontend\nqueue table didn't know to refetch. Dispatch the 'queue-entry-updated'\nevent on both delete and restore so the service queues UI stays in sync.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3076],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"efc6d8f527acc021de816ff8f85d7015a0b48137","date":"2026-02-24T14:29:38.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve mark deceased/alive workflows (#3050)","message":"(fix) Improve mark deceased/alive workflows (#3050)\n\n* (fix) Improve mark deceased/alive workflows\n\nReplace window.location.reload() with targeted SWR cache invalidation in both the mark-deceased form and mark-alive modal. After toggling death status, the patient data, current visit, and visit/encounter caches are revalidated so the UI updates reactively without a full page reload.\n\nAlso adds death date validation against the patient's date of birth: the date picker now sets minDate to the patient's birth date, and a Zod refine rejects death dates before DOB. The backend already has this check in PersonValidator, but the frontend was not enforcing it, allowing the user to submit and get a generic error toast.\n\nUpdates the warning text from \"will end any active visits\" to \"updates this patient's death information\" since the current /person endpoint does not actually close visits.\n\n* Update markDeceasedWarning translation to match component","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3050],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"ebb3f1156a112c4e6eae3a1c2917e77fe5aa8acd","date":"2026-02-24T13:43:57.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5447: Use encounter's own visit context when editing (#3056)","message":"(fix) O3-5447: Use encounter's own visit context when editing (#3056)\n\nWhen editing an encounter from a past (closed) visit, the form entry\ncomponent was using the active visit's context instead of the\nencounter's actual visit. This caused the backend to reject edits with\n\"The encounter datetime should be between the visit start and stop\ndates.\"\n\nThis commit fixes the issue by fetching the encounter's visit via a\nlightweight SWR call when `encounterUuid` is present, and gate form\nrendering until the data resolves. For visitless encounters, the visit\ncontext is correctly left null rather than falling back to the active visit.","ticketKeys":["O3-5447"],"pullRequests":[3056],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"ee157646a8d93be7ced49d8a0eaa341ed67321d3","date":"2026-02-06T22:50:28.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Disable test results refresh button while revalidation is in-flight","message":"(fix) Disable test results refresh button while revalidation is in-flight\n\nPrevent duplicate refresh requests by tracking the refresh state and\ndisabling the button until all SWR revalidations have settled.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"11fef2c97a225178fd0051c62fae6523432f2128","date":"2026-02-05T20:24:05.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Use targeted SWR cache invalidation for test results refresh (#2998)","message":"(fix) Use targeted SWR cache invalidation for test results refresh (#2998)\n\nReplace `window.location.reload()` with SWR cache mutation to refresh\ntest results data without a full page reload. Iterates over cache keys\ndirectly rather than using a filter function, since SWR's `mutate()`\nwith a filter explicitly skips `$inf$`-prefixed keys from\n`useSWRInfinite` hooks.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2998],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"21b4b98ddcea58e5ba3ec71fa8f974c47359bd41","date":"2026-02-05T17:37:27.000Z","author":"Souravjyoti Dutta","subject":"(fix) O3-5319: Refresh test results viewer after saving lab results (#2983)","message":"(fix) O3-5319: Refresh test results viewer after saving lab results (#2983)","ticketKeys":["O3-5319"],"pullRequests":[2983],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"03d6a5b9a61e3bc255cfa1281dc9d488f1ffd469","date":"2026-02-03T09:11:56.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Fix delete visit modal receiving undefined visit prop (#2985)","message":"(fix) Fix delete visit modal receiving undefined visit prop (#2985)\n\n* (fix) Fix delete visit modal receiving undefined visit prop\n\nThe delete visit modal expected an `activeVisit` prop but callers passed\nvisit, causing the modal to receive `undefined`. This rename also\nremoves the redundant `mutateActiveVisit` callback, since\n`invalidateVisitAndEncounterData` already handles SWR revalidation.\n\nThis change also adds unit tests for the delete visit action item component\nand an e2e test for deleting a visit from the visit history table.\n\n* Use dynamic birthdate in e2e test patient fixture\n\nUse a dynamically computed birthdate (5 years ago) instead of a\nhardcoded '2020-2-1' date. The hardcoded date caused test failures\nas time passed because age-dependent reference ranges and UI logic\nwould shift relative to the fixed date.\n\n* Make patient birthdate deterministic without timezone conversion\n\nBuild the birthdate as a YYYY-MM-DD string based on the current year.\nAvoids UTC conversion drift from toISOString in e2e tests.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2985],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart"],"revisions":["HEAD"],"messageTerms":["problem list","problem-list","reload","refresh","SWR","invalidate","visit note conditions"],"count":30},"coverageGaps":[],"truncated":["commits: answer byte cap reached; showing 18 of 30 found"]}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LvhXSTcyGn1Zu2a5EbfKp4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
